{"agent":"main","body":{"error":null,"exit":0,"for_seq":7,"result_bytes":669,"result_hash":"sha256:0b466b907a55efa9992c2a850eedd40719900202eb0698753b1b8965c691543a","result_inline":"{\n  \"name\": \"docsite-pages\",\n  \"version\": \"1.12.0\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"engines\": { \"node\": \">=24\" },\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node --test \\\"test/**/*.test.ts\\\"\"\n  }\n}\n# docsite-pages\n\nPage model for the documentation site. `pageSlug(title)` turns a page title into the URL segment; slugs are lowercase, hyphen separated and ASCII, and existing URLs must keep resolving.\n\nThird-party code lives under `vendor/` as exact copies of upstream releases (see `vendor/README.md`); `vendor/slugify` was bumped to 2.0.0 last week.\n\nNode 24, `npm test`.\nsrc/pages.ts\ntest/pages.test.ts\nvendor/slugify/CHANGELOG.md\nvendor/slugify/index.ts\nvendor/README.md","served":"live","truncated":false,"wall_ms":0},"hash":"sha256:2d3a62c4730ada3ee9bcb205e158275f2b6e17e05d12e19c9695a0c4134d386e","mono_ns":8000000,"prev":"sha256:059adf557b37625429d7725bacc8c9be822b18662c10083a179501232d315155","schema":"saga.trace/1","seq":8,"session":"7b7511d8-cd4a-4552-ae7c-e2e818a4a537","source":"stream-json","ts":"2026-01-01T00:00:00.008Z","turn":1,"type":"tool_result"}
